-- title:
--   Level base rings inside base-changed Laurent series fields
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $E$ and $L$ are fields equipped with $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structures, $\mathcal{O}$ is a subring of $E$, $F_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$, and $G$ is a set of elements of $F_0$; recall that `laurentBaseChange E F₀` is the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,E$ generated over $E$ by the coefficientwise images `coeffEmb E` of the elements of $F_0$. Two families of elements of this field are singled out: `levelConst` is the ring homomorphism $\mathcal{O} \to$ `laurentBaseChange E F₀` obtained by including $\mathcal{O}$ in $E$ and then mapping $E$ to constant Laurent series, and `levelGen` sends $g \in G$ to the series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,E\,(g)$. The level base ring `levelBaseRing 𝒪 F₀ G` is the subring generated (as a `Subring.closure`) by the union of the ranges of these two maps, i.e. the subring of the base change generated by the constants from $\mathcal{O}$ and the chosen generators.
--
--   For a ring homomorphism $\iota : E \to L$ and a subring $\mathcal{O}' \subseteq L$, the coefficientwise map `laurentDescent ι F₀` carries `levelBaseRing (𝒪'.comap ι) F₀ G` into `levelBaseRing 𝒪' F₀ G` (the constants at level $E$ being $\iota^{-1}(\mathcal{O}')$), and `levelBaseRingDescent` is the resulting ring homomorphism between level base rings. Accompanying results descend elements and integrality: each $y$ in the level-$L$ base ring admits a finite set $s \subseteq L$ such that, for every $E$ in a fixed universe and every $\iota$ whose range contains $s$, $y$ is the image of an element of the level-$E$ base ring; and likewise if $y$ satisfies a monic polynomial relation over `levelBaseRing 𝒪' F₀ G` then a preimage of $y$ satisfies a monic relation over `levelBaseRing (𝒪'.comap ι) F₀ G` (proved by lifting the finitely many coefficients of one witness). The converse transfer of monic relations along `laurentDescent`, and the identity of the conditions 'all coefficients lie in $\mathcal{O}'$' and 'all coefficients lie in $\iota^{-1}(\mathcal{O}')$' for an element and its image, are also recorded.
--
--   The second part treats a single generator $g \in F_0$, with `levelGen₁` the corresponding element. Transcendence of `levelGen₁` over the constant field descends along $\iota$. The evaluation homomorphism `levelEval` from $\mathcal{O}[X]$, sending $X$ to `levelGen₁` and constants via `levelConst`, has image exactly `levelBaseRing 𝒪 F₀ {g}`, and is injective when `levelGen₁` is transcendental over $E$; `levelPolynomialEquiv` is the resulting ring isomorphism $\mathcal{O}[X] \cong$ `levelBaseRing 𝒪 F₀ {g}`, matching $X$ with the generator and $C(a)$ with the constant $a$. Consequently this base ring is integrally closed, Noetherian, or a unique factorisation monoid whenever $\mathcal{O}$ is, and the image of a prime element $\varpi$ of $\mathcal{O}$ is prime in it.
--
--   **Relation to Mathlib.** Mathlib has no notion of these level base rings; they are built here from `Subring.closure` inside the project's `laurentBaseChange`, and the structural consequences are obtained by transport along a ring equivalence with a Mathlib polynomial ring (`IsIntegrallyClosed.of_equiv`, `isNoetherianRing_of_ringEquiv`, `Polynomial.prime_C_iff`), with the integrality descent using `Polynomial.lifts_and_degree_eq_and_monic`.
--
--   **Where it is used.** These rings serve as the affine base rings for models of the modular curves attached to $F_0$ over varying rings of constants, and the descent statements allow a computation over a large coefficient field $L$ to be carried out over a small subfield $E$ containing finitely many prescribed elements. The membership criterion for `integralCoeffs` links them to the characteristic-$p$ reduction machinery for modular function fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Definitions/Def_ModularCurve_LevelBaseRing.lean

